'''Nedre Romerike''' is the lower (southern) part of the [[Romerike]] [[districts of Norway|traditional district]] in [[Akershus]], [[Norway]]. It consists of the municipalities [[Lillestrøm]], [[Lørenskog]], [[Nittedal]], [[Rælingen]] and [[Aurskog-Høland]]. It make up the area served by [[Nedre Romerike District Court]], based in [[Lillestrøm (town)|Lillestrøm]]. The upper (northern) half of Romerike is known as [[Øvre Romerike]].<ref>{{cite web|url =  https://snl.no/Nedre_Romerike |title= Nedre Romerike|publisher =  Store norske leksikon	|author=  Svein Askheim
|accessdate=September 1, 2018}}</ref>
<ref>{{cite web|url =  https://snl.no/Romerike|title= Romerike|publisher =  Store norske leksikon |author=  Svein Askheim|accessdate=September 1, 2018}}</ref>
